---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Leaf from '../components/illustrations/Leaf.astro';
import PathLine from '../components/illustrations/PathLine.astro';

const contactEmail = 'chesterbeard@salishseaconsulting.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · HarvestMap"
  description="Who runs HarvestMap, why it exists, where the farm data comes from, and how every listing is reviewed."
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: var(--space-7); max-width: 760px;">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow"><Leaf class="is-drawn" style="width:18px;height:18px;" /> About the map</span>
      <h1 class="squiggle squiggle-pine">Why HarvestMap exists</h1>
      <p class="lead">Finding a good u-pick farm shouldn't require four tabs, three forums, and a guess. HarvestMap brings the farms to one place, organized by what's actually in season.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
      <h2 style="margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2);">Who runs it</h2>
      <p>
        HarvestMap is built and maintained by Chester Beard through
        <a href="https://www.salishseaconsulting.com" rel="noopener">Salish Sea Consulting</a>. It started as a simple
        idea — a directory that answers one question well: <em>"who is harvesting what, near me, right now?"</em> — and
        grew into a national map of small farms, orchards, farm stands, and farmers markets.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2);">Where the data comes from</h2>
      <p>Our listings start from a few public sources, and we confirm each farm's details against its own website or phone before we publish it:</p>
      <ul style="padding-left: var(--space-5);">
        <li><strong>USDA Local Food Portal</strong> — a public directory of farms, markets, and food businesses across the country.</li>
        <li><strong>PickYourOwn.org</strong> — a long-running community resource that helped us find u-pick farms and orchards.</li>
        <li><strong>Grower submissions</strong> — farms that list themselves or send us a "what's ripe" update directly.</li>
        <li><strong>The farm's own website</strong> — the source we check for crops, hours, and contact details before a listing is marked as verified.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        A farm that came from a public directory may not have photos or detailed seasonality yet. We mark those listings
        honestly so you know what's been verified and what hasn't.
      </p>

      <h2 id="why-some-states" style="margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2);">Why some states aren't listed yet</h2>
      <p>
        We only publish a state when we can show you at least four farms we've checked. A checked farm has a confirmed
        crop list, a working website or phone number, and real visitor details like hours or activities.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some states have plenty of farms in public directories but very little we can confirm. Rather than show you a page
        full of names and addresses, we hold those states back until the data is good enough to use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Right now that includes Alaska, Hawaii, Iowa, Kansas, Maryland, Montana, Nevada, North Dakota, South Dakota, Utah,
        Wyoming, and a few others. We add states as we verify more farms.
      </p>
      <p>
        Grow in one of these states? <a href="/add-farm">List your farm</a> and you'll help put it on the map.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2);">How we review listings</h2>
      <p>
        Every grower submission is reviewed by a real person before it goes live — usually within 48 hours. We check the
        basic facts, clean up anything confusing, and follow up by email if we have questions. This is deliberate: no
        self-serve dashboard, no instant anonymous edits. A little friction keeps the directory trustworthy.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2);">A word on accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Farms change their hours, their crops, and their minds. Seasonal availability on HarvestMap is estimated from
        growing zones and crop calendars — it is not a promise from the farm. Always call ahead before you drive out,
        especially during shoulder seasons.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="container" aria-hidden="true" style="margin: var(--space-6) 0;">
      <div class="divider">
        <span class="divider__seed"><Leaf /></span>
        <PathLine class="is-drawn" />
        <span class="divider__seed"><Leaf /></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel panel--feature" style="text-align: center;">
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;">
        A product of <a href="https://www.salishseaconsulting.com" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--clay-deep);">Salish Sea Consulting</a>.
        Questions or corrections? Email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} style="color: var(--clay-deep);">{contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
